LMA SoulX-Podcast DSP research library (not registered in the APK)

dsp.cpp translates audio feature, conditional flow and source-excitation
operations reviewed in Soul-AILab/SoulX-Podcast and xingchensong/S3Tokenizer.
Those projects are Apache-2.0; relevant upstream attributions include
Soul-AILab contributors, Alibaba Inc., OpenAI and Tsinghua University.
LMA adaptations: Copyright 2026 LMA contributors, Apache-2.0.
The API header and build/test tooling are original LMA MIT-licensed code.
The Apache license is provided in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.

The separately downloaded, pinned KISS FFT source is BSD-3-Clause,
Copyright (c) 2003-2010 Mark Borgerding. The original license is provided in
LICENSE-KISSFFT-BSD-3-CLAUSE. It is linked into the ignored build archive only;
neither that archive nor the library is distributed in the current APK.

Host checks AST-extract pinned torchaudio (BSD-2-Clause) and librosa (ISC)
Python function bodies into memory and read the publisher's S3 mel bank from
the ignored checkout. They are test references only, not App model assets.
Their wheels, binaries, copied function files, example audio, model-specific
filter banks and checkpoints are not included in the public source or APK.
See third_party/soulx-dsp-source-lock.json and docs/SOULX_DSP.en.md for pins,
test boundaries and the still-missing complete model pipeline.
